<Base title="How CalcsDesk will show its working | Methodology" description="The CalcsDesk standard for source references, visible assumptions, reproducible calculations and tested official examples." breadcrumb="Methodology">
  <article class="reading-page"><p class="eyebrow">The working, not just the answer</p><h1>Every number should<br />have an explanation.</h1><p class="lead">CalcsDesk is being built around a simple standard: you should be able to see what a calculation uses and how it reaches a result.</p><div class="notice"><strong>Development status</strong><p>The first wage-only federal income-tax tool is available as a beta, with sourced 2026 rate data and automated schedule checks. Human review and the full calculator release checklist remain pending. Other calculators are in preparation.</p></div><h2>Start with the right context.</h2><p>Choose the country and relevant region, then the tool. The finished calculation will state the tax year or effective period, currency, pay frequency and any eligibility assumptions.</p><h2>Use traceable rates.</h2><p>Before a tool is released, each changeable rate must have an official source URL and a verification date. The calculation page will link to the rate table it uses. A source-directory link by itself does not mean a rate has been verified.</p><h2>Test the working.</h2><p>Each calculator must reproduce at least two official worked examples before full release. The federal beta currently has official tax-schedule cross-checks and tests of the wage portions of IRS Medicare examples; those do not replace the full worked-example gate. Its tests must also cover relevant thresholds, rounding, invalid inputs and important edge cases.</p><h2>Explain the limits.</h2><p>The result will include the formula, a breakdown, inputs, assumptions and exclusions. Estimates are not tax, legal or financial advice, and may differ from a payroll system or an individual filing outcome.</p><h2>Keep the calculation local.</h2><p>The intended calculator flow runs in the browser without sending your entered figures to a server. These development pages do not collect financial inputs. The theme preference is saved on this device when browser storage is available.</p><h2>Check before relying on a result.</h2><p>Until a tool’s rates and official examples are verified, it stays in preparation. Verification labels and reviewer credentials will be shown only when the corresponding work has actually happened.</p><a class="text-link" href="/sources/">Explore official reference sources →</a></article>
</Base>
